# Optional. A source build needs no env file at all: `vp i && vp run dev` starts a
# local server that only reachable clients can pair with. Do not add server-side
# secrets to this file.
#
# Everything here is read at build time by a client bundle, or by a native mobile
# build. The web and desktop apps never reach a hosted account or relay.

# Desktop updates: which GitHub repository the updater checks for a newer release.
# Defaults to the repository CI built this build from.
# T3CODE_DESKTOP_UPDATE_REPOSITORY=owner/repo

# Release train reported in local diagnostics ("stable", "nightly", "preview",
# "dev"). Official release workflows set this; local builds and forks use "dev".
# T3CODE_TELEMETRY_CHANNEL=dev

# Mobile only, and the mobile app's cloud surface is still upstream's (TS9 owns it).
# These are public client identifiers, not secrets; get your own from your account.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE=t3-relay
# T3CODE_RELAY_URL=https://relay.example.test

# Public, ingest-only mobile OpenTelemetry configuration.
# T3CODE_MOBILE_OTLP_TRACES_URL=https://api.axiom.co/v1/traces
# T3CODE_MOBILE_OTLP_TRACES_DATASET=t3-code-mobile-traces-dev
# T3CODE_MOBILE_OTLP_TRACES_TOKEN=xaat-...
